## Chapter 15: The Joint Sector Assessment Begins
The fog in Sector-C East was thick enough to taste—damp, smelling of pulverized concrete and old moss.
Renna led the team down a collapsed four-lane avenue. Her tower shield was raised high, her boots stepping deliberately through the rubble. Mina hovered three paces to the left, her sharp eyes scanning the shattered windows of the five-story apartment blocks lining the street. Tobias brought up the rear, his heavy crossbow loaded and resting against his shoulder.
Kaelen walked just behind Renna’s right shoulder, carrying a coil of rusted steel wire and a pouch of low-grade impact flares. To anyone watching through the camera drones drifting overhead through the mist, he looked like a nervous, overburdened pack-mule trying not to trip over his own feet.
"Hold up," Mina whispered, dropping into a low crouch near a overturned transit bus. She held up two fingers. "Movement in the alley. Two targets... no, three."
A sharp, clicking sound echoed off the damp brick walls. Three **Rubble-Stalkers**—dog-sized, eight-legged beasts covered in sharp, jagged concrete-like plates—emerged from the fog. They were Tier-E monsters, worth 1 point each.
"Standard formation!" Renna ordered softly, planting her shield. "Tobias, take the lead target. Mina, watch the flank. Kaelen, stay behind me!"
"G-Got it!" Kaelen stuttered, ducking low behind Renna’s iron tower shield.
Tobias fired. The crossbow bolt struck the first Stalker square in its stone-like skull, shattering its shell and dropping it instantly. The remaining two beasts snarled, springing forward. Renna stepped into their path, her shield absorbing the impact with a heavy, metallic *CLANG*, while Mina darted in from the side, her daggers biting deep into the exposed joints of the second beast.
While Renna and Mina engaged, Kaelen's **[Hive-Mind Synapse]** flared sharply in the back of his skull.
A cold, heavy vibration pulse rippled through his boot insoles. It wasn't coming from the three Rubble-Stalkers. It was coming from deeper within the Sector-C ruins, moving rapidly toward their position.
Kaelen tilted his head subtly. His **[Low-Light Spatial Perception]** cut through thirty meters of dense fog and concrete wreckage.
Two hundred meters away, near the border separating Sector-C from the commercial ruins of Sector-B, a squad of Gideon Prep students was frantically retreating. Behind them, crashing through a brick wall like a battering ram, was a monster that had no business being in an outer training grid.
A **Granite-Scale Behemoth**.
**[Monster Identification: Granite-Scale Behemoth (Tier-C)]**
 * **Attributes:** Extreme Mass Density, Kinetic Absorbing Hide, Trample Rampage.
 * **Threat Assessment:** Lethal to non-specialized frontline units. Capable of collapsing concrete structures.
The Gideon squad—panicking after failing to hold Sector-B—had deliberately diverted the Tier-C beast toward the outer perimeter to break its pursuit, dumping the high-tier monster straight onto Anvil Ridge’s sector.
"Hey!" Tobias yelled, dropping the third Rubble-Stalker. "Look at the radar map! Something big just entered our quadrant!"
"What?" Renna whirled around, checking her wrist monitor. The warning icon was flashing bright crimson. "That's a Tier-C signature! Why is a Sector-A target in the outer perimeter?"
Before she could finish her sentence, the brick wall at the end of the avenue exploded outward in a shower of flying mortar and stone.
The Granite-Scale Behemoth burst into the street. It stood ten feet tall, resembling a massive, armored bull covered in interlocking slabs of granite-hard bone. Its eyes blazed with a manic, blood-red light as it let out a deafening roar that shattered the remaining glass in the surrounding apartment windows.
"Fall back! Fall back into the narrow alley!" Renna screamed, her face going pale as she braced her shield. "Tobias, Mina, move!"
The Behemoth lowered its heavy horn, its massive hooves tearing up the asphalt as it accelerated directly toward Renna’s squad. In this open street, its trample rampage would crush Renna’s tower shield like a tin can.
Kaelen’s eyes narrowed beneath his lowered hood.
Camera drones were sweeping through the upper fog, but the dense dust cloud from the collapsed wall created a three-second blind spot right behind Renna's position.
*Three seconds,* Kaelen calculated silently.
He didn't run. As Renna stepped forward to take the suicidal impact, Kaelen reached out with his left hand, grabbing the back of her tactical vest. With a gentle, perfectly calculated pull using a tiny fraction of his **38 Strength**, he yanked her backward off her footing, making it look as if she had slipped on the loose gravel.
"Whoa—!" Renna stumbled backward, her shield tilting wildly.
In that exact microsecond, as the dust cloud swallowed the space between them and the charging beast, Kaelen activated his stored skill.
"**[Kinetic Overdrive]**!"
A silent, invisible shockwave exploded through Kaelen's nervous system. His reaction time sped up by 50%, the world around him dropping into a absolute crawl. The charging ten-foot Behemoth seemed to freeze mid-stride, every floating particle of dust hanging suspended in the air.
Kaelen stepped around Renna’s falling frame in a blur that left zero visual trail.
He closed his right fist, the concealed high-density bracer under his sleeve locking against his wrist. He didn't use a wild, flashy magic strike. He drove a short, compact straight punch directly into the Behemoth's lower knee joint—the exact structural focal point where all its forward momentum was concentrated.
*BOOM!*
The impact sounded like a cannon firing inside a closed room.
Kaelen’s **38 Strength**, amplified by the 25% armor-shattering bonus of **[Kinetic Overdrive]** and his **[Plated Chitin Framework]**, shattered the monster's granite knee-cap into powder.
The Behemoth’s massive leg collapsed instantly under its own twelve-ton momentum. The beast didn't trample the squad—it violently flipped over itself, plowing face-first into the asphalt and sliding twenty feet through the rubble, crashing headlong into a steel support pillar before going completely still.
Kaelen disengaged **[Kinetic Overdrive]** instantly, his speed dropping back to baseline before the dust cloud cleared.
He tumbled backward onto his rear right beside Renna, scrambling frantically in the dirt, clutching a rusted iron pipe and screaming at the top of his lungs with deliberate, hysterical terror.
"AAAAH! IT CRASHED! IT CRASHED!" Kaelen yelled, flailing his arms like a terrified child.
The dust settled.
Renna scrambled up onto her knees, holding her shield, her eyes wide with absolute shock. Tobias stood frozen with his crossbow halfway lifted, his jaw practically touching his chest. Mina stared from the alley mouth, her daggers shaking in her hands.
In the center of the shattered street lay the Tier-C Granite-Scale Behemoth, its massive leg twisted at an impossible angle, its skull buried four feet inside a collapsed steel pillar, dead.
"What... what just happened?" Tobias stammered, pointing a trembling finger at the carcass. "Did... did it trip?"
Renna looked down at Kaelen, who was sitting in the dirt, breathing heavily, clutching his knees and shivering. Then she looked at the shattered asphalt where the beast’s leg had collapsed.
"The asphalt gave way under its weight," Renna breathed, her voice filled with disbelief as she looked at the massive trench carved into the street. "It was charging too fast... the old sewer pipe beneath the road collapsed under its rear leg."
"Talk about an insane stroke of luck," Mina gasped, running over and helping Renna up. "A Tier-C beast just killed itself on the terrain!"
Kaelen pulled himself up slowly, wiping mud from his cheek, his face wearing a look of pale, lingering shock.
"I... I thought we were dead," Kaelen muttered, his voice trembling convincingly.
Renna patted his shoulder firmly, her amber eyes filled with relief. "You pulled me back, Kaelen. If you hadn't pulled my vest, I would have taken that charge head-on. You saved my life."
"I just... panicked and pulled," Kaelen stammered, lowering his head.
While Renna and Tobias cheered, celebrating their unbelievable survival, Kaelen casually walked toward the rear of the dead Behemoth, placing his bare palm against its hidden flank where the dust was still thick.
In the quiet dark of his mind, he whispered the command:
"**[Dissect & Assimilate]**."
The dark gray vapor flared beneath his palm, devouring the dense Tier-C carcass from the underside, silently extracting its high-density essence while his squad was busy scanning the horizon.
